81:func writeRootHelp(writer io.Writer) error {
82:	_, err := fmt.Fprint(writer, `Grimoire is a unified repository discovery interface over source, documentation, Lexicon symbols, and Arcana relationships.
83:
84:Usage:
85:  grimoire <command> [flags]
86:
87:Core workflow:
88:  grimoire model setup                 Install the local embedding runtime
89:  grimoire model start                 Start the managed embedding service
90:  grimoire index --root .              Prepare source and Lexicon-aligned chunks
91:  grimoire knowledge index --root .    Index repository rationale and documentation
92:  grimoire knowledge search --query .  Retrieve cited documentation with BM25 and vectors
93:  grimoire vector build --root .       Build or refresh documentation vectors
94:  grimoire eval knowledge --cases ...  Judge documentation retrieval against a frozen corpus
95:  grimoire eval arcana --cases ...     Compare Arcana graph retrieval with and without vectors
96:  grimoire orient --root .             Discover compact repository anchors
97:  grimoire search --root . --query ... Search independent evidence lanes
98:  grimoire trace --anchor <id>         Expand an exact structural handle
99:  grimoire inspect --handle <id>       Read exact source or documentation
100:  grimoire lexicon doctor --repo .     Run language-analysis diagnostics
101:  grimoire arcana sync                 Synchronize structural graph state
102:  grimoire mcp --root .                Serve the unified discovery tool over stdio
103:
104:Commands:
105:  orient    Discover compact source and symbol anchors
106:  search    Search exact, source, documentation, and symbol lanes; defer graph expansion
107:  trace     Expand bounded structural paths from a returned handle
108:  impact    Find bounded incoming or outgoing dependents
109:  inspect   Read exact evidence for returned handles
110:  query     Compatibility entry point for the discovery modes
111:  index     Prepare repository source state
112:  status    Inspect or prepare repository analysis state
113:  knowledge Index, search, inspect, or vectorize repository knowledge
114:  lexicon   Run direct Lexicon analysis, adapter, snapshot, and diagnostic commands
115:  arcana    Run direct Arcana graph, synchronization, and structural commands
116:  vector    Build or inspect documentation vector state
117:  investigation  Create, inspect, or close an agent investigation ledger session
118:  mcp       Serve the unified repository discovery tool over stdio
119:  model     Set up and manage the embedding runtime
120:  eval      Run judged retrieval evaluation
121:  version   Print the Grimoire version
122:  help      Show this help
123:
124:Lexicon and Arcana remain independently usable components. Grimoire uses their
125:repository-local state automatically during discovery and also exposes their
126:specialist commands under grimoire lexicon and grimoire arcana.
127:`)
128:	return err
129:}
